  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 218 PM CDT Thu Aug 6 2026\n\nSaturday another short wave will bring additional chances for \nstorms, mainly into the evening and overnight.  These storms will \ngenerally have similar support to Friday night, and we'll need to \nwatch for both heavy rain and strong wind gusts.  \n\nSunday and beyond, west/northwest flow is forecast to continue \naloft, with our region near the edge of any heat dome in the Plains. \nThis is a active region any time of year, and one where short waves \naloft should arrive periodically. These are difficult to time out at \nthis point, but the outlook for active storm chances continues \nthrough mid week, along with seasonally warm/humid conditions in the \n80s and dew points values in the lower/mid 70s.",
